  "title": "The density vanishes Hⁿ-a.e. off the carrier (Upper Density Theorem)",
  "statement": "Let P, n ∈ ℕ, S ∈ 𝒟_n(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ n), and let R = (M, θ, ξ) be an integer multiplicity representation of S in ℝ^P (R : IMRep univ n with R.Represents S; M = R.carrier). Let Θ : ℝ^P → ℝ satisfy HasMassDensity S x Θ(x) for every x ∈ ℝ^P. Then H^n({x ∈ ℝ^P : x ∉ M and Θ(x) > 0}) = 0, where H^n = μHE[n] (evaluated as an outer measure).",
  "lean_statement": "∀ (P n : ℕ) (S : GeometricCurrentOn (univ : Set (Euclid P)) n) (R : IMRep (univ : Set (Euclid P)) n) (Θ : Euclid P → ℝ), R.Represents S → (∀ x : Euclid P, HasMassDensity S x (Θ x)) → (μHE[n] : Measure (Euclid P)) {x | x ∉ R.carrier ∧ 0 < Θ x} = 0",
